<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/discharge-planning-for-inpatients-without-previous-diabetes-diagnosis> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Discharge Planning for Inpatients Without Previous Diabetes Diagnosis" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Inpatients without a previous diagnosis of diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "discharge-planning-for-inpatients-without-previous-diabetes-diagnosis" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "When an inpatient is discharged from hospital on steroid therapy a clear strategy for the management of hyperglycaemia or potential hyperglycaemia should be in place. The titration of therapy to address the hyperglycaemia should be communicated to the GP or community DSNs in the discharge letter. Similarly, the risk of hypoglycaemia and the appropriate de-escalation of therapy when steroid doses are reduced or withdrawn should also be part of the communication strategy." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "When an inpatient is discharged from hospital on steroid therapy a clear strategy for the management of hyperglycaemia or potential hyperglycaemia should be in place. The titration of therapy to address the hyperglycaemia should be communicated to the GP or community DSNs in the discharge letter. Similarly, the risk of hypoglycaemia and the appropriate de-escalation of therapy when steroid doses are reduced or withdrawn should also be part of the communication strategy." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_08_hyperglycaemia_and_steroid_therapy_january_2023> .

