<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/steroid-induced-diabetes> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Steroid Induced Diabetes" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "The guideline recommends monitoring capillary glucose in people at risk of steroid induced diabetes and initiating treatment if glucose levels exceed 12.0 mmol/L." ;
    dmo:name "Steroid Induced Diabetes" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "steroid-induced-diabetes" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "At the commencement of corticosteroid therapy in people considered at risk of steroid induced diabetes, capillary glucose (CBG) testing should be initiated once daily." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_08_hyperglycaemia_and_steroid_therapy_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/steroid-therapy> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Steroid Therapy" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Steroid therapy is a modifiable risk factor for hyperglycaemia and diabetes, as it can be initiated, adjusted, or discontinued based on clinical need." ;
    dmo:name "Steroid Therapy" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "steroid-therapy" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "The use of steroid treatment in people with pre-existing diabetes will undoubtedly result in worsening glucose control; this may be termed steroid induced hyperglycaemia. This warrants temporary additional and more active glycaemic management." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_08_hyperglycaemia_and_steroid_therapy_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/treatment-with-sulphonylureas-meglitinides-or-insulin> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Treatment with Sulphonylureas, Meglitinides or Insulin" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Following a hospital admission care must be taken to ensure the safety of individuals when steroid doses are lowered to reduce the risk of hypoglycaemia in those treated with sulphonylureas, meglitinides or insulin." ;
    dmo:name "Treatment with Sulphonylureas, Meglitinides or Insulin" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "treatment-with-sulphonylureas-meglitinides-or-insulin" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Following a hospital admission care must be taken to ensure the safety of individuals when steroid doses are lowered to reduce the risk of hypoglycaemia in those treated with sulphonylureas, meglitinides or insulin." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_08_hyperglycaemia_and_steroid_therapy_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/twice-daily-steroid-therapy> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Twice Daily Steroid Therapy" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Twice daily steroid therapy may require more intensive insulin regimens such as a basal bolus regimen due to persistent hyperglycaemia throughout the day." ;
    dmo:name "Twice Daily Steroid Therapy" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "twice-daily-steroid-therapy" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If so, seek advice from the diabetes specialist team as it is likely that hyperglycaemia is likely to be persistent throughout the day and that more intensive insulin regimens will be required such as a basal bolus regimen." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_08_hyperglycaemia_and_steroid_therapy_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/use-of-diabetes-risk-calculator> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Use of Diabetes Risk Calculator" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Document mentions use of a diabetes risk calculator (e.g. University of Leicester/Diabetes UK) to identify those at risk, indicating it is a method of risk assessment." ;
    dmo:name "Use of Diabetes Risk Calculator" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "SocioDemographic" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "use-of-diabetes-risk-calculator" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "• Those identified to be at risk utilising an appropriate diabetes risk calculator e.g. University of Leicester/Diabetes UK (www.riskscore.diabetes.org.uk – last accessed 18/11/22)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_08_hyperglycaemia_and_steroid_therapy_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/use-of-glucocorticoid-steroids> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Use of Glucocorticoid Steroids" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "The use of glucocorticoid steroids is becoming more widespread and can impact adversely on glycaemic management in individuals with or without a previous diagnosis of diabetes." ;
    dmo:name "Use of Glucocorticoid Steroids" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "use-of-glucocorticoid-steroids" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "The use of glucocorticoid steroids is becoming more widespread. Use of these medications can impact adversely on glycaemic management in those individuals living with diabetes and others without a previous diagnosis of diabetes." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_08_hyperglycaemia_and_steroid_therapy_january_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/acute-hyperglycaemia> a dmo:Symptom ;
